hubs (153: 334 events/253 partners, 5th most active node; 407: 120 events/106 partners - steps 12, 13), which is the classic confounder producing time-ignoring connectivity without transmission. Critically, no available tool exposes event timestamps, so I could not verify monotonic time ordering or the <=600-unit inter-contact gaps within [28025, 66424]. Every link on the path is a single non-repeating contact (repeat ratio 0.034, step_01), leaving exactly one possible realisation whose timing is unknown. The evidence establishes reachability but not a time-respecting cascade; I decline to call it present or absent."}, "raw_final_response": "## Investigation summary\n\n**What I could establish:**\n- The graph has 16,325 events over [4, 100000], 15,767 distinct edges, repeat ratio 0.034 \u2014 i.e. almost every pair interacts exactly once (step_01).\n- 695 is a very low-activity node: 6 events, 6 distinct partners, only **two** out-edges (\u2192407, \u21921468), and its 695\u2192407 contact happened exactly once (step_02, step_03, step_10).\n- 1495 has 11 events and only 4 in-neighbours: 627, 1512, 1517, 1541 (step_04).\n- There is **no direct** 695\u21921495 edge (step_16).\n- A static directed path does exist: 695\u2192407 (step_10), 407\u2192153 (step_14), 153\u21921541 (step_11), 1541\u21921495 (step_15). That is a 4-hop chain, and every link on it is a single, non-repeating contact.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the intermediaries on that path are exactly the kind of hubs that manufacture spurious \"connectivity\" \u2014 153 has 334 events / 253 partners (5th most active node overall), 407 has 120 events / 106 partners, 1566 has 128 (step_12, step_13). So the existence of the path is largely explained by hub degree, not by a genuine transmission chain.\n\n**What I could not establish:** none of the available tools return event timestamps or per-edge time lists. I therefore have no way to check the two properties that actually define the claim: (a) that the four contacts occur in increasing time order, and (b) that each successive contact follows the previous one by \u2264600 units, all inside [28025, 66424]. With every edge firing only once, the chain has exactly one candidate realisation, and the probability that four independent single-shot contacts happen to fall in order within 600-unit gaps inside a 38,399-unit window is low a priori \u2014 but that is a prior, not evidence.\n\nConclusion: the time-ignoring connection is real but hub-mediated; the temporal constraint is untested and untestable with the instrumentation available.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 407, 153, 1541, 1495],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.5,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"695 and 1495 are not directly connected (step_16). A static directed 4-hop path exists: 695->407->153->1541->1495 (steps 10, 14, 11, 15), and 695's only out-edges are to 407 and 1468 (step_03) while 1495's only in-neighbours are 627/1512/1517/1541 (step_04), so this is essentially the sole candidate route. However, the route runs through high-degree hubs (153: 334 events/253 partners, 5th most active node; 407: 120 events/106 partners - steps 12, 13), which is the classic confounder producing time-ignoring connectivity without transmission. Critically, no available tool exposes event timestamps, so I could not verify monotonic time ordering or the <=600-unit inter-contact gaps within [28025, 66424]. Every link on the path is a single non-repeating contact (repeat ratio 0.034, step_01), leaving exactly one possible realisation whose timing is unknown. The evidence establishes reachability but not a time-respecting cascade; I decline to call it present or absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 33943, "total_output_tokens": 6304, "total_tokens": 40247, "total_latency_ms": 91120, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}